  "notes": "NAME ORIGIN:\n{親|おや} (parent) + {子|こ} (child) + {丼|どん} (rice bowl) → \"parent and child bowl\"\nThe name comes from the combination of chicken (parent) and egg (child).\n\nINGREDIENTS:\n- {鶏肉|とりにく} (chicken)\n- {卵|たまご} (egg)\n- {玉|たま}ねぎ (onion)\n- {醤油|しょうゆ} (soy sauce)\n- みりん (sweet cooking sake)\n- {出汁|だし} (dashi broth)\n- ご{飯|はん} (rice)\n\nCOOKING TIP:\nThe egg should be slightly runny ({半熟|はんじゅく}) for the best texture.\n\nRELATED {丼|どんぶり} DISHES:\n- カツ{丼|どん} (pork cutlet rice bowl)\n- {牛丼|ぎゅうどん} (beef rice bowl)\n- {天丼|てんどん} (tempura rice bowl)\n- {海鮮丼|かいせんどん} (seafood rice bowl)",
